          "level": 1,
          "content": "8 WORKING WITH FRACTIONS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.829,
            0.185,
            0.877,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "0774CH08"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.792,
            0.093,
            0.913,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.298,
            0.578,
            0.322
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8.1 Multiplication of Fractions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.332,
            0.516,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "Aaron walks 3 kilometres in 1 hour. How far can he walk in 5 hours?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.369,
            0.517,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": "This is a simple question. We know that to find the distance, we need to find the product of 5 and 3, i.e., we multiply 5 and 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.447,
            0.499,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered in 1 hour = 3 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.472,
            0.262,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.496,
            0.433,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered in 5 hours"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.28,
            0.525,
            0.388,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "= 5 \\times 3    km",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.561,
            0.438,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": "3+3+3+3+3 \\mathrm{km}",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.524,
            0.366,
            0.819,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.453,
            0.598,
            0.543,
            0.616
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "= 15 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.64,
            0.851,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": "？ Aaron’s pet tortoise walks at a much slower pace. It can walk only $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ kilometre in 1 hour. How far can it walk in 3 hours?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.69,
            0.848,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": "Here, the distance covered in an hour is a fraction. This does not matter. The total distance covered is calculated in the same way, as multiplication."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.757,
            0.707,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.892,
            0.52,
            0.92
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered in 1 hour $= { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } }$ km."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
